Keep the audit trail in MySQL when the real-time index is off

piler 1.4.6 moved the audit records to the Manticore real-time index audit1,
and AUDIT() returns early when RT=0. An installation on the plain Sphinx index
(as grommunio Archive is) therefore records no audit trail at all, and the
audit viewer, the CSV export and the per-hour download/restore limits query an
index that does not exist, hiding the existing records in the MySQL audit
table. With RT=0, write and read the MySQL audit table as piler 1.3.x did; the
RT=1 code paths are unchanged.

